    "created_at": "2016-03-11T21:31:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-11T21:31:08Z",
    "body": "Agreed, we should make the attribute reflect the actual used value. So for elements where \"\" is treated as \"no value was provided\" we should make the reflected attribute indicate that.\n\nI'd say that more often than not, treating \"\" as \"no value was provided\" is the more expected behavior by developers. It'd be nice if we were somewhat consistent about that.\n",
